      "source_text": "19. it received a suffix rather than forcing the rest of the sequence to be renamed A checksum was generated after transfer to the archive server, and a second copy was written to offline storage. The project log recorded the operator, capture date, equipment settings and any unusual page condition Access Copy Versus Original Evidence Text recognition was treated as an access aid, not a replacement for the image. Handwriting quality varied widely. and technical abbreviations often confused automated systems. Staff therefore created a short verified transcription only for titles, dates. locations and selected measurements Search users could find a notebook through those fields and then inspect the original page image. Where a number was uncertain, the transcription included a visible uncertainty marker rather than silently choosing a value By the end of the first month, 2,480 pages had been captured from thirly-six notebooks The team intentionally avoided setting a daily page quota because fragile material required different handling times. Instead. quality was reviewed through weekly sample checks of focus, sequence, colour reference and file integrity This slower but controlled workflow preserved the relationship between the digital files and the physical notebooks, which was more important than maximizing the number of scans completed each day",
